      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present an unusual case of verified myocardial infarction without surgery. Successful elective lumbar spine surgery was performed 4 days post-myocardial infarction during perioperative beta-blockade, after cardiology evaluation recommended surgery without further evaluation. Clinical and ethical considerations are discussed."},
